# chatkeys.walk (order 1612): Enter inside an open chat, then Back.
#
# Window 23's hang walk lost one Back frame on the line (1613) and its next
# Enter came inside the open chat, where the shared key table's Enter opens
# the message under the cursor (1076): a detail view the M9 does not draw,
# which its [PAGE] line called `chat`. Every Back after it closed that
# unseen view and every Enter opened it again, five minutes on one chat
# with every key read. Since 1612 the M9 closes such a state at once and
# says it (`[UI] notice="unshown=detail closed"`), so one Back leaves.
#
# The window 23 probe of the same name opened the list's first row, a chat
# with no message (`[OPEN] peer=f18f4927 messages=0`), where Enter has
# nothing to open; it passed on the broken image. This one opens "Bench"
# after an arrival, so the cursor stands on a message. On an image before
# 1612 it fails at the last wait; from 1612 on it passes.
#
#   just m9-walk <rig> scripts/m9-walks/chatkeys.walk <bench elf>
allow key_ms 2000

bench arrive
key enter
wait page=chat
dump in-chat
key enter
expect log "unshown=detail"
dump after-enter-in-chat
key back
wait page=chats
dump after-back
idle 6
